docs {
  # roster-demographics.readonly endpoint access (ONEROSTER-58)

  One request asks for an LEA token holding only the `roster-demographics.readonly` scope.
  `runScopeAccess` (in `lib/scope-access.js`) checks that the token holds exactly that
  scope, then calls every endpoint in `lib/access-matrix.js` with it and expects:

  - `/demographics` to return HTTP 200 with the `demographics` collection
  - every other endpoint to return HTTP 403 in the `imsx_*` error envelope, with no data

  Each endpoint is its own named test, e.g. `roster-demographics.readonly › users → 403`.
  The token is only used inside the request, so `lea-odsApiToken` is left untouched.
}
